+
+# todo-check 行號驗證重查 Design
+
+This is not a design for new work. It is the record `plan`'s own tooling
+needs — `ledger.js lint` requires a `**Spec:**` file to open — for a task
+whose premise turned out to be false.
+
+## What the task asked
+
+`todo-check 不驗 path:line 的行號：改成不存在的行仍然 exit 0
+（scripts/todo-check.js）`, sourced from `.fankeel/build/survey.md`, which
+itself read: "linksIn strips everything after # and only ever calls
+fs.existsSync(full); no line-count check exists anywhere in the file."
+
+## What is actually in the tree
+
+- `git log --oneline -- scripts/todo-check.js` — the newest commit is
+  `02d32348 feat: todo-check rejects a path:line whose line is past the
+  file's end`, landed 2026-09-25.
+- A manual repro from the repo root — a `TODO.md` fixture citing
+  `scripts/todo-check.js` at a line number far past its end, once as a
+  backtick span and once as a markdown link — reports `past end` and exits 1
+  in both forms, not 0.
+- `node --test tests/todo-check.test.js` — 62 pass, 0 fail, including
+  `tests/todo-check.test.js:65-76`, two fixtures built for exactly this
+  citation-past-the-end case.
+- `TODO.md` carries no open entry for this; it only describes the check in
+  prose (`TODO.md:55`). `docs/README.md:144-145,149` and
+  `docs/decisions/2026-09-25-todo-line-and-multiplier.md` already record the
+  delivery.
+
+## Conclusion
+
+The bug named by the task does not exist in the current tree — it was fixed
+the day before this session, tested, and archived
+(`docs/archive/2026-09-25-todo-line-and-multiplier.md`). `survey.md`'s claim
+is stale. Nothing in `scripts/todo-check.js` needs to change, so the plan
+this design feeds has zero tasks.
+
+against the map: `.fankeel/map.md:77` — no conflict; `todo-check.js`'s listed
+responsibility ("whether TODO.md is still an index") is unchanged.
